{
  "anchor": "font-feature-settings-prop",
  "content": "| Name:                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| normal [&#124;](CSS-VALUES-4#comb-one) [\\<feature-tag-value>](CSS-FONTS-4#feature-tag-value)[#](CSS-VALUES-4#mult-comma) |\n| normal                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| all elements and text                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| yes                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| n/a                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| as specified                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| per grammar                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| discrete                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n\nTests\n\n*   [font-features-across-space-1.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-1.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-1.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-1.html)\n*   [font-features-across-space-2.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-2.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-2.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-2.html)\n*   [font-features-across-space-3.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-3.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-3.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-features-across-space-3.html)\n*   [font-feature-settings-tibetan.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-feature-settings-tibetan.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-feature-settings-tibetan.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-feature-settings-tibetan.html)\n*   [font-feature-settings-computed.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-computed.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-computed.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-computed.html)\n*   [font-feature-settings-invalid.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-invalid.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-invalid.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-invalid.html)\n*   [font-feature-settings-valid.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-valid.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-valid.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-feature-settings-valid.html)\n\nThis property provides low-level control over OpenType font features. It is intended as a way of providing access to font features that are not widely used but are needed for a particular use case.\n\nAuthors should *not* use [font-feature-settings](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-feature-settings) to set any of the font features in the table below. Instead, please use the higher-level replacement properties, because:\n\n1.  The higher-level properties cascade individually. You can set one without setting the whole [font-feature-settings](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-feature-settings) list\n2.  Some higher-level properties can be synthesized for fonts that do not support the font feature.\n\n| If you want to set this font feature                         | then use this *instead of* [font-feature-settings](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-feature-settings)                                                                                               | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Kerning (`kern`) or Vertical Kerning (`vkrn`)                | [font-kerning](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-kerning): [normal](CSS-FONTS-4#font-kerning-normal-value)                                                                  | The [font-kerning](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-kerning) property will set the `kern` or `vkrn` feature depending on the [writing-mode](CSS-WRITING-MODES-4#propdef-writing-mode). |\n| Standard Ligatures (`liga`) or Contextual Ligatures (`clig`) | [font-variant-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-ligatures): [common-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-ligatures-common-ligatures)               |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Discretionary Ligatures (`dlig`)                             | [font-variant-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-ligatures): [discretionary-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-ligatures-discretionary-ligatures) |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Historical Ligatures (`hlig`)                                | [font-variant-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-ligatures): [historical-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-ligatures-historical-ligatures)       |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Contextual Alternates (`calt`)                               | [font-variant-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-ligatures): [contextual](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-ligatures-contextual)                           |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Subscript (`subs`)                                           | [font-variant-position](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-position): [sub](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-position-sub)                                            |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Superscript (`sups`)                                         | [font-variant-position](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-position): [super](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-position-super)                                        |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Small Capitals (`smcp`)                                      | [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps): [small-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-caps-small-caps)                                          |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Small Capitals From Capitals (`c2sc`)                        | [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps): [all-small-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-caps-all-small-caps)                                  |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Petite Capitals (`pcap`)                                     | [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps): [petite-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-caps-petite-caps)                                        |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Petite Capitals From Capitals (`c2pc`)                       | [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps): [all-petite-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-caps-all-petite-caps)                                |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Unicase (`unic`)                                             | [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps): [unicase](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-caps-unicase)                                                |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Titling (`titl`)                                             | [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps): [titling-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-caps-titling-caps)                                      |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Lining Figures (`lnum`)                                      | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [lining-nums](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-lining-nums)                               |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Oldstyle Figures (`onum`)                                    | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [oldstyle-nums](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-oldstyle-nums)                           |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Proportional Figures (`pnum`)                                | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [proportional-nums](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-proportional-nums)                   |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Tabular Figures (`tnum`)                                     | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [tabular-nums](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-tabular-nums)                             |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Fractions (`frac`)                                           | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [diagonal-fractions](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-diagonal-fractions)                 |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Alternative Fractions (`afrc`)                               | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [stacked-fractions](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-stacked-fractions)                   |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Ordinals (`ordn`)                                            | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [ordinal](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-ordinal)                                       |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Slashed Zero (`zero`)                                        | [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric): [slashed-zero](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-numeric-slashed-zero)                             |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Historical Forms (`hist`)                                    | [font-variant-alternates](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-alternates): [historical-forms](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-alternates-historical-forms)            |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Stylistic Alternates (`salt`)                                | [font-variant-alternates](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-alternates): [stylistic()](CSS-FONTS-4#stylistic)                                                       | Define which alternate gets used by making an [@font-feature-values](CSS-FONTS-4#at-ruledef-font-feature-values) rule                                                                                    |\n| Character Variant 1 - Character Variant 99 (`cv01` - `cv99`) | [font-variant-alternates](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-alternates): [character-variant()](CSS-FONTS-4#character-variant)                                       | Define which character variant gets used by making an [@font-feature-values](CSS-FONTS-4#at-ruledef-font-feature-values) rule                                                                            |\n| Swash (`swsh`) or Contextual Swash (`cswh`)                  | [font-variant-alternates](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-alternates): [swash()](CSS-FONTS-4#swash)                                                               | Define which swash gets used by making an [@font-feature-values](CSS-FONTS-4#at-ruledef-font-feature-values) rule                                                                                        |\n| Ornaments (`ornm`)                                           | [font-variant-alternates](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-alternates): [ornaments()](CSS-FONTS-4#ornaments)                                                       | Define which ornament gets used by making an [@font-feature-values](CSS-FONTS-4#at-ruledef-font-feature-values) rule                                                                                     |\n| Alternate Annotation Forms (`nalt`)                          | [font-variant-alternates](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-alternates): [annotation()](CSS-FONTS-4#annotation)                                                     | Define which annotation gets used by making an [@font-feature-values](CSS-FONTS-4#at-ruledef-font-feature-values) rule                                                                                   |\n| JIS78 Forms (`jp78`)                                         | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [jis78](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-jis78)                                  |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| JIS83 Forms (`jp83`)                                         | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [jis83](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-jis83)                                  |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| JIS90 Forms (`jp90`)                                         | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [jis90](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-jis90)                                  |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| JIS2004 Forms (`jp04`)                                       | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [jis04](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-jis04)                                  |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Simplified Forms (`smpl`)                                    | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [simplified](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-simplified)                        |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Traditional Forms (`trad`)                                   | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [traditional](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-traditional)                      |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Full Widths (`fwid`)                                         | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [full-width](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-full-width)                        |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Proportional Widths (`pwid`)                                 | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [proportional-width](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-proportional-width)        |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| Ruby Notation Forms (`ruby`)                                 | [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian): [ruby](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-variant-east-asian-ruby)                                    |                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n\n> **Example:** For example, there is no font-variant value to control Scientific Inferiors (small numerals used in chemical formulae). Readability is enhanced by using them, so they must be enabled using font-feature-settings:\n>\n> ```\n> .chem {\n>   font-feature-settings: 'sinf'\n> }\n> ```\n>\n> ![scientific inferior numbers in a chemical formula](images/scientific-inferiors.png)\n>\n> Scientific inferiors improve readability of chemical formulae\n\n> **Note:** The entire property value is set at once. Unlike the font-variant properties, there is no way to modify the inherited value by adding or removing individual features.\n\nA value of **normal** means that no change in glyph selection or positioning occurs due to this property.\n\nFeature tag values have the following syntax:\n\n```\n<feature-tag-value> = <opentype-tag> [ <integer [0,∞]> | on | off ]?\n<opentype-tag> = <string>\n```\n\nThe [\\<opentype-tag>](CSS-FONTS-4#typedef-opentype-tag) is a case-sensitive OpenType feature tag. As specified in the OpenType specification \\[OPENTYPE\\], feature tags contain four ASCII characters. Tag strings longer or shorter than four characters, or containing characters outside the U+20–7E codepoint range are invalid. Feature tags need only match a feature tag defined in the font, so they are not limited to explicitly registered OpenType features. Fonts defining custom feature tags should follow the [tag name rules](https://www.microsoft.com/typography/otspec/featuretags.htm) defined in the OpenType specification \\[OPENTYPE-FEATURES\\].\n\nFeature tags not present in the font are ignored; a user agent must not attempt to synthesize fallback behavior based on these feature tags. The one exception is that user agents may synthetically support the kern feature with fonts that contain kerning data in the form of a `kern` table but lack kern feature support in the `GPOS` table.\n\n> **Note:** In general, authors should use the [font-kerning](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-kerning) property to explicitly enable or disable kerning since this property always affects fonts with either type of kerning data.\n\nIf present, a value indicates an index used for glyph selection. An [\\<integer>](CSS-VALUES-4#integer-value) value must be 0 or greater. A value of 0 indicates that the feature is disabled. For boolean features, a value of 1 enables the feature. For non-boolean features, a value of 1 or greater enables the feature and indicates the feature selection index. A value of **on** is synonymous with 1 and **off** is synonymous with 0. If the value is omitted, a value of 1 is assumed.\n\nThe computed value of font-feature-settings is a map, so any duplicates in the specified value must not be preserved. If the same feature tag appears more than once, the value associated with the last appearance supersedes any previous value for that axis.\n\nThe computed value contains the de-duplicated feature tags, sorted in ascending order by [code unit](INFRA#code-unit).\n\n> **Example:** ```\n> font-feature-settings: \"sinf\" 1;       /* sinf=1 enable Scientific Inferiors */\n> font-feature-settings: \"sinf\" on;      /* sinf=1 enable Scientific Inferiors */\n> font-feature-settings: 'sinf';         /* sinf=1 enable Scientific Inferiors */\n> font-feature-settings: \"sinf\" off;     /* sinf=0 disable Scientific Inferiors */\n> font-feature-settings: \"sinf\", 'twid'; /* sinf=1, twid=1 enable Scientific Inferiors and Third Widths */\n> font-feature-settings: \"sinf\" \"twid\";  /* invalid, need a comma-delimited list */\n> font-feature-settings: \"silly\" off;    /* invalid, tag too long */\n> font-feature-settings: \"PKRN\";         /* PKRN=1 enable custom feature */\n> font-feature-settings: sinf;           /* invalid, tag must be a string */\n> ```\n\nWhen values greater than the range supported by the font are specified, the behavior is explicitly undefined. For boolean features, in general these will enable the feature. For non-boolean features, out of range values will in general be equivalent to a 0 value. However, in both cases the exact behavior will depend upon the way the font is designed (specifically, which type of lookup is used to define the feature).\n\nImplementations may choose to ignore turning off features which the OpenType specification says are always required, such as required ligatures \"rlig\".\n\nTests\n\n*   [font-variant-ligatures-11.optional.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-variant-ligatures-11.optional.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-variant-ligatures-11.optional.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-variant-ligatures-11.optional.html)\n\nAlthough specifically defined for OpenType feature tags, feature tags for other modern font formats that support font features may be added in the future. Where possible, features defined for other font formats should attempt to follow the pattern of registered OpenType tags.\n\n> **Example:** The Japanese text below will be rendered with half-width kana characters:\n>\n> ```\n> body { font-feature-settings: \"hwid\"; /* Half-width OpenType feature */ }\n>\n> <p>毎日カレー食べてるのに、飽きない</p>\n> ```",
